  13:34:10-13:34:38  received 792 of 860 expected (~92%)
  link_dropped_total=0: the loss is between Discord and ears. Short utterances lost
  most of their audio with no pause recorded (3/23, 18/34, 18/35, pauses=0). Whether
  packet loss was injected wasn't confirmed.
Results
  Stop recording me ...................... PASS (stops at once, in core and ears)
  Agree again ............................ PASS (capture back within the second)
  Audio % ................................ BORDERLINE (~91-92%)
  Second speaker ......................... NOT TESTED (was on the list, never spoke)
  Overall ................................ PARTIAL
Follow-up
  - Owner asked whether gaps are just pauses (D&D has long pauses). They aren't
    counted: ears ends a piece of speech after 800 ms of silence, so pauses only split
    speech. These losses are inside utterances.
  - Read-aloud test scripts added so audio and speech-to-text can be judged against
    known words and pauses: docs/test-scripts/ (#119, PR #123).
  - Reviews of the scripts found: #120 (capture check can drop audio counts), #121
    (ears may cut the start of each piece of speech), #109 comment (stop drops speech
    still being transcribed).

