2026-10-05  Test 1, run 5: DM alone, free talk (meant to be the script)
==============================================================================
Setup       development @ 75ec854 (#135), whisper-local small, DMBOT_DEBUG_AUDIO=1. The
            DM alone; read the reminder message aloud and talked instead of the script.
Timeline (UTC)
  18:35:37  Session started; consent list: 2 opted in; joined voice; notice posted
  18:35-18:36  Capture checks 96%, 100%, 100%; no ⚠️
  18:36:25  Whisper started a 1.04 s clip and started nothing else for 40 s
  18:37:16  /dmbot stop
Numbers     ears: 3389 of 3394 packets (99.9%), link_dropped_total=0, 15 audio lines.
            One 22 s piece (10 short pauses, 1.7 s total) was cut at core's 15 s cap.
Results
  Audio % ................................ PASS (99.9%)
  Reminder shows the new wording ......... PASS (read aloud; Whisper wrote "Anyone on
                                           this can read what you write down")
  Speech-to-text keeps up ................ FAIL: 40 s stall on a 1 s clip (#137)
  Overall ................................ PARTIAL (no script, so no transcript score)
Found
  - #137 local Whisper can take ~40 s on a 1 s clip and stall every clip behind it.
  - Seen live: #120 (capture checks due at ~18:36:49 and ~18:37:04 never posted, their
    audio counts dropped) and #109 (a 13 s clip still queued at stop was dropped).
  - #138 /dmbot help still says players use /consent give to agree.
  - "Count to three" didn't make 0.8 s of silence, so a pause didn't split the speech.
  - "One person" means the DM alone: one-person.md had Player lines. Replaced with
    dm-only.md, and dramatic pauses became "mute, count to three, unmute" (#139, #140,
    PR #141).

